   "core/parsers/frankie_ecom.py - FRANKIE ECOM colour x size grid.\n\nWELL WORN / COSTCO TAIWAN ECOM variant (e.g. PO# DW20250807E-S26 - FRANKIE #1399):\n\n    XS S M L XL XXL Total Units Cartons            <- size header\n    BLEACH (LIGHT BLUE) 40 40 40 40 160 4 $8.35 $1,336.00   <- colour row\n    OASIS (MEDIUM BLUE)  40 40 40 40 160 4 $8.35 $1,336.00\n    Total Per Size       80 80 80 80 320 8 $2,672.00         <- sum row\n\nKey differences from matrix_percarton (FRANKIE JAPAN/KOREA/TAIWAN INLINE):\n\n  * the size columns ALREADY carry TOTAL UNITS (40 each, not per-carton);\n  * \"Total Units\" is the real per-colour row total (160) - used for cross-check;\n  * \"Cartons\" (4) is packaging only and is IGNORED;\n  * unit is forced to PCS - our base unit is PCS, never Carton.\n\nThe grid is located structurally, so the recipe only pins ``layout_type`` and the\nparser needs no anchors - making the layout fully cacheable (zero AI on re-runs,\nno confirm dialog).\n",
